          }
        ],
        "node": "wait"
      },
      {
        "when": [
          {
            "if": "questDone",
            "quest": "dinners_out",
            "not": true
          }
        ],
        "node": "offer"
      },
      {
        "when": [
          {
            "if": "flag",
            "flag": "talked_hatch",
            "not": true
          }
        ],
        "node": "first"
      },
      {
        "when": [
          {
            "if": "flag",
            "flag": "talked_hatch",
            "eq": 1
          }
        ],
        "node": "second"
      },
      {
        "node": "third"
      }
    ],
    "nodes": {
      "shut": {
        "lines": [
          "The shutter's down and bolted from inside. A card on it: NO HOT FOOD AFTER THE BELL. Under it, smaller, in pencil: or before it, some nights.",
          "The range behind it is ticking as it cools."
        ]
      },
      "offer": {
        "lines": [
          "Somebody behind the hatch is scraping a pan. \"You're not on the rota, love.\" The scraping stops. \"Never mind. Three tins want taking out to the signalmen on Cinder Walk.\"",
          "\"They won't come in for them. They never have. One at the foot of each signal, the dead ones. Don't knock on the post, and don't wait to be thanked.\""
        ],
        "options": [
          {
            "label": "I'll take them",
            "actions": [
              {
                "do": "quest",
                "quest": "dinners_out"
              },
              {
                "do": "give",
                "item": "signal_dinner",
                "qty": 3
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "label": "Not now"
          }
        ]
      },
      "wait": {
        "lines": [
          "\"One tin at each dead signal on Cinder Walk, love. Lids on. They'll be cold before you're halfway down the Walk. They always are, and I send them hot anyway.\""
        ]
      },
      "in": {
        "lines": [
          "The shutter goes up a hand's width. \"All three? You're quicker than the last one.\" A jar comes out across the counter, the lid wired down.",
          "\"Get that down you, love. It's a lot of walking, the Works, and nobody feeds you out there but me.\""
        ],
        "options": [
          {
            "label": "Thank you",
            "actions": [
              {
                "do": "handin",
                "quest": "dinners_out"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "first": {
        "lines": [
          "\"Five dinners at twelve, love, same as ever. Plated and covered, and on the counter by five past. Five come back full.\"",
          "\"They go back on the shelf at one, and I do five again in the morning. Somebody has to keep the range in.\""
        ],
        "actions": [
          {
            "do": "flag",
            "flag": "talked_hatch",
            "value": 1
          }
        ]
      },
      "second": {
        "lines": [
          "\"The night shift was to be relieved at six. It's there on the rota, in red. I don't write the rota, love. I only read it.\"",
          "\"I read it out to the yard of a morning, the whole sheet. Then I put the kettle on.\""
        ],
        "actions": [
          {
            "do": "flag",
            "flag": "talked_hatch",
            "value": 2
          }
        ]
      },
      "third": {
        "lines": [
          "\"There's knocking in that pipe in the yard, some nights. Three, and a rest, and three.\"",
          "\"I don't answer it. I did once, with a spoon on the iron, and it went on till it was light.\""
        ]
      },
      "more": {
        "lines": [
          "\"Dropped them? I've more. I always do too many, it's a habit you get in a canteen. Bring us a lump of coal for the range and they're yours.\""
        ],
        "options": [
          {
            "label": "A lump of coal for three tins",
            "actions": [
              {
                "do": "take",
                "item": "coal",
                "qty": 1
              },
              {
                "do": "give",
                "item": "signal_dinner",
                "qty": 3
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "label": "Not now"
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  },
  "canteen_pipe": {
    "speaker": "Pipe Mouth",
    "start": [
      {
        "when": [
          {
            "if": "questReady",
            "quest": "what_the_pipes_say"
          }
        ],
        "node": "in"
      },
      {
        "when": [
          {
            "if": "questActive",
            "quest": "what_the_pipes_say"
          }
        ],
        "node": "wait"
      },
      {
        "when": [
          {
            "if": "questDone",
            "quest": "what_the_pipes_say",
            "not": true
          }
        ],
        "node": "offer"
      },
      {
        "node": "after"
      }
    ],
    "nodes": {
      "offer": {
        "lines": [
          "An iron pipe comes up out of the yard and ends in an open flange, about the height of my ear. So I put my ear to it.",
          "Knocking, a long way down: three, a rest, three. Then nothing, for as long as it takes to say it, and again. A plate on the flange: TO SLAG MERE."
        ],
        "options": [
          {
            "label": "Find where it comes up",
            "actions": [
              {
                "do": "quest",
                "quest": "what_the_pipes_say"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "label": "Leave it"
          }
        ]
      },
      "wait": {
        "lines": [
          "Three, a rest, three. TO SLAG MERE. There are more pipe mouths at the mere. I'm to listen at them for where it's loudest."
        ]
      },
      "in": {
        "lines": [
          "The pipe's quiet. I keep my ear on the cold iron a while longer to be sure, and count three and three in my head."
        ],
        "options": [
          {
            "label": "It's stopped",
            "actions": [
              {
                "do": "handin",
                "quest": "what_the_pipes_say"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "after": {
        "lines": [
          "TO SLAG MERE. Quiet now. The iron's cold against my ear, and a long way down there's water moving."
        ]
      }
    }
  },
